		{
			description: [
				"The Atroxiia is an ancient cryomancy-adapted lindworm species inhabiting frozen mountain ranges, glacial valleys, and polar frontiers. Rather than overwhelming prey through relentless pursuit, Atroxiia establish dominance by exerting precise control over the terrain itself, reshaping the battlefield through specialized cryomantic abilities channeled primarily through the tail. Their composed temperament, territorial discipline, and unusually regal demeanor have inspired countless legends depicting them as forgotten monarchs or divine guardians of winter, though such accounts remain unverified. Despite their measured behavior, an Atroxiia becomes exceptionally dangerous once provoked, relying on calculated force rather than prolonged aggression. &4&nAny meetings will likely be hostile.&r"
				"Before an Atroxiia can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Atroxiia become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 60 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4raw cod, salmon, beef, porkchops, mutton, chicken, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
				"Feeding an Atroxiia does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/atroxiia.png width:481 height:113 align:center}"
			]
